hing because it's all going to  cook together and then bacon is going to  be the third item i love bacon because  it just gives that smokiness and a  secret with this bacon is it doesn't  look quite raw that's because i  microwaved it for 90 seconds  when you add bacon to a skewer sometimes  the bacon doesn't cook all the way and  so if you give it a good head start um  then by the time everything cooks it  will be crispy which is what we're  looking for so i'm gonna build these  skewers and then we'll get them on the  grill okay i'm getting the last of these  skewers built they're nice and heavy and  they're going to be fantastic have your  grill heated to about medium medium high  don't have it all the way up because you  want these to cook kind of slow we want  our chicken to get cooked all the way  through before  they burn i have this cool indoor grill  that i'm going to use  but cook them for like four or five  minutes per side flip it over cook the  other side  and  mainly you just want your chicken to be  done so if you're worried about it just  put a thermometer in there 160 degrees  so we'll cook these until that point  okay these have been cooking about four  or five minutes per side i got about 155  160 on my thermometer you can find these  thermometers at your local smiths  you can have pick up deliver those to  you actually if you wanted one at your  house  let me put these on a plate these are so  full of flavor they don't even need a  sauce i promise you you can find all  these ingredients at your local smiths  thank you so much for watching thank you  for shopping have a happy memorial day  bye bye everybody  thank you to smith's food and drug for  sponsoring this segment for more  information visit smithfoodanddrug.com  now over to you mercedes
 

